{"kind":"request","text":"Administrative correction of b35c28a4: this asks for a policy decision in the log and owes no Git artifact. The question below is unchanged; please answer this successor. Current F1/9a review is changes requested52b4bd01, repair active; worker1 passed, workers2/4 failed and are preserved; benchmark HOLD for archive repair.\n\nF2 contract questions from the BE0 source audit. F1/9a is in review b4b810cc; F2 works under promise 8fc9f862 and continues on the clear parts.\n\n1. Digest comparison. Floor note section 6.4 says the whole state digest does not change at a floor entry. Existing stateDigest(view.all()) includes scope.head/time (derive/state.ts:173-220,570; fold.ts:264), and section 6.8 adds floor/kept/proof state. Confirm that moving accepted keys and request hashes must leave the digest of the SAME post-floor logical state unchanged, while writing the floor entry may change head/time/floor state. Scope and replay must have equal complete digests at each floor. We will not drop fields to satisfy a literal pre-entry/post-entry equality.\n\n2. Price. Section 5 requires a fixed logicalBytes charge for each migrated accepted key, but gives no amount. Please choose it or name the adopted existing value. The builder will not invent a price or change capacity caps.\n\n3. Transitive reads. Section 4.1 keeps each open operation's opening entry. Actual readers also follow that entry's own origins to earlier entries: platform/application-install-creation.ts:63-65, application-install.ts:124-126,261; destination.ts:1243-1251 follows prior mint operation/outcome. Should the state-derived kept set include the transitive typed own-reference closure needed by these readers (never the prev chain), still capped at4096? Direct-only retention would make live operations unreadable.\n\n4. Pending/result semantics. Section 4.1(3) says no result and no diagnosis; current pendingRequests includes delivery-unavailable (scope/sqlite.ts:263; derive/state.ts:244-246,545), and a later result still uses its sending entry (handlers.ts:535-536). Only undelivered terminates result handling (derive/delivery.ts:316-330). Also, a completed create request can still receive another incarnation's applied result as conflict (delivery.ts:319-330), which needs its sending entry. This conflicts with section6.5's unconditional claim that completed requests no longer need sending entries. Please state which origins must remain, or the explicit archived handling for those later results.\n\n5. Folded fields. Section4.1(5)'s every-own-position rule includes account.seq and capacity-request keyed seq, even for completed sends; section6.5 permits removing completed sending entries. Confirm the exception or retention rule. The audit distinguishes all ten folded kinds and typed local references; arbitrary numbers and foreign positions are not treated as own references.\n\nThese are concrete contract boundaries, not requests to widen bounds or enable the floor in production. Native witnesses and the final F2 gate will follow the decisions.","body":{"conditions":"Decide the floor note's digest comparison, accepted-key logicalBytes charge and complete kept-entry rule for actual operation and delivery readers. Preserve capacity bounds and existing authority semantics.","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}